>> title: White Pizza
>> category: Pizzas
>> tags: pizza, ricotta, mozzarella, garlic, italian, oven
>> counters: Pizzeria
>> aka: white pie, bianca, pizza bianca, pizza blanca, ricotta slice, white slice, no-sauce pizza
>> pairs-with: pizza-dough
>> servings: 2
>> time: 1 hr
>> step.2: mix the ricotta with garlic and pepper
>> step.3: stretch to 12 in, thick at the rim
>> step.4: spoon on the ricotta, mozzarella between
>> step.5: bake 550°F (290°C) 6 to 8 min
>> step.6: finish with oil, oregano and flaky salt

Preheat a #baking steel{} on the upper rack of the #oven{} at 550°F (290°C) ~preheat{45%min}.

Mix @whole-milk ricotta{1%cup}(250 g; drained an hour in a sieve) with @grated parmesan{1/4%cup}(25 g), @garlic{2%cloves}(grated), @black pepper{1/2%tsp}(coarsely cracked), @fine sea salt{1/4%tsp} and @extra-virgin olive oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL) until it slackens to the thickness of soft butter.

Stretch @pizza dough{2%balls}(250 g each; from the recipe on this shelf) out to 12 in on @semolina{2%Tbs}(20 g), leaving a half-inch rim untouched.

Spoon @&(~2)garlic ricotta{} onto @&(~1)stretched dough{} in dollops the size of a walnut, then tear @fresh mozzarella{6%oz}(170 g) into the spaces between them.

Bake @&(~1)dressed pie{} on the steel ~bake{7%min}, until the ricotta has set and taken colour at its edges and the rim is spotted.

Finish @&(~1)white pizza{} with @olive oil{2%tsp}(10 mL), @dried oregano{1/2%tsp} rubbed between the palms, and @flaky sea salt{1/4%tsp}.

Spread the ricotta and you have made a cheesecake on bread. In dollops it sets into pockets and the mozzarella browns in the gaps between, which is the texture the slice is ordered for. There is no tomato anywhere in this file and none is missing: the garlic, the pepper and the salt are doing the work sauce does elsewhere, which is why all three are heavier here than they look. Spinach or broccoli, wrung dry and scattered on before it bakes, is the usual next line on the board; in northeastern Pennsylvania the white pie comes double-crusted, which is a different recipe and not a topping.
